      "question": {
        ":question/id": "8f321ac9-ee74-5d56-a034-80aecb67e54f",
        ":question/problem": "Use the substitution $u=x^{2} + 3$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int x e^{x^{2} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=x^{2} + 3$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int x e^{x^{2} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "6e195de5-18d2-5700-a7e5-20c251a0b310",
            ":answer-field/key": "answer",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "2c90b6df-19e0-5f7f-b549-9ace0f4c2c60",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "- \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)"
              },
              {
